<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-cingo</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to enclose around</i>, <i>surround</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā Mons Apenninus regiones Italiae
					Etruriaeque circumcingit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					2, 6, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eum zonā gloriae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ecclus. 45, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">PORTICVS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4043</span></i>
			.—In <i>part. pres.</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 7,
			15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">telis circumcingentibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					10, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
